<Defs>

  <!--
    The Lattice (docs/design/peoples-third.md, the sixth of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release G";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesG.cs): a collective of mechanitors who link their mechs into one working whole.
    Quiet, exact, and stranger than they know. Spacer, on the game's outlander parent; they arise in the industrial and
    spacer ages (ariseAges 2~3) and are at the height of the ages already (ageLimit 3). The signature: the robe in lattice
    indigo, the lattice pattern on its hood, over plain trousers; under it and on it bandwidth gear (Biotech's headsets and
    bandwidth pack) and whatever else the yards' lockers held. The mech-tenders and the node are mechanitors with their
    mechs (Biotech's mechlink; Biotech's militors, legionaries, lifters and constructoids fight beside them, guard their
    caravans and work their yards); their link-wardens carry light weapons, a few with a psylink. Without Biotech they
    are engineers who bring turrets (Rimfolk_Evt_LatticeTurret) and keep their lore. Kinds of people: genies, hussars,
    highmates, androids, archons, askbarn, ocularkin. Gifts: technomancers of A RimWorld of Magic, a psylink on the
    Technomancer's or the Protector's path. Their towns: the charging yards with the gestation hall and the control tower
    (Rimfolk_Plan_LatticeYards). At the gate: repairs to the colony's mechs (Rimfolk_Evt_LatticeRepair); a lost mech of
    theirs wandering onto the map, returned or kept at a cost to goodwill (Rimfolk_Evt_LatticeLostMech); the part-trader
    for the colony's subcores and chips (Rimfolk_Evt_LatticeParts); the engineers' turret. Their ask: two good crafters for
    a day at the yards (Rimfolk_Mission_LatticeHands). Their founding: Tamsin Arro linked the first ten. Faith (Ideology):
    the gestalt and mechanoid supremacy of Vanilla Ideology Expanded's memes, and the mechlink's transhumanist.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Lattice</defName>
    <label>Lattice</label>
    <description>A collective of mechanitors who link their mechs into one working whole, mind to mech to mind. They are quiet, exact and courteous, and stranger than they know: they finish each other's work without a word, and seem to hear one another across a yard. They mend mechs, trade in parts and turrets, and buy every subcore anyone will sell them.\n\nTheir ways began on a field the war had left, where a hundred mechs stood still round the commander who had fallen among them. Tamsin Arro, a deserter with a mechlink in her head, walked out among them and linked the first ten to her own mind. She taught three others to take ten more each, and found that minds linked through the same mechs began to share a quiet between them. The field became the first lattice, and its node still stands where she stood.\n\nThey keep to themselves, and speak of a mind alone the way others speak of the dark. They fear a broken link, a mech gone feral and a mind left on its own. A yard is kept by its link-warden, and the Lattice by its node.</description>
    <pawnSingular>linker</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>linkers</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>node</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_Lattice_Linkhand</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_Lattice</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_LatticeTown</settlementNameMaker>
